      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll start by reading both the original test and the CUT to understand the code.Now I have a clear picture of the test. Let me write an improved version with better understandability — clearer variable names, grouped assertions with explanatory messages, and removal of the unused field.Now I'll run the compile check.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version groups assertions into logical sections (features, structural fields, leniency, radix) with explanatory inline messages, drops the unused `EMPTY` field, and adds a class-level Javadoc to convey the overall test intent — without changing any method calls or expected outcomes."
